---
source: crates/gamepadii/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help(&[\"leds\"])"
---
The per-button RGB LEDs: animation, brightness, colours and the custom theme. Over the control channel when the firmware has the LED commands (no reboot); else from web-config, where stock firmware doesn't show the animation or brightness (in a gamepad mode the control channel takes the pad there and back)

Usage: gamepadii leds [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  set         Change the LEDs live, with no reboot (needs control channel v1.1 of the gamepadii firmware). RAM only unless --save: the pad goes back to its saved LED settings when it restarts
  brightness  One brightness step up or down, or a level, live (as `set --brightness`)
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - human:  Text for people
          - json:   The versioned JSON contract ("schema": 1)
          - waybar: One line of waybar custom-module JSON; `status` and `leds` only
          
          [default: human]

      --json
          Same as `--format json`

      --stay
          Leave the pad in web-config afterwards instead of rebooting it back into its gamepad mode

      --host <HOST>
          Talk to the web configurator at HOST (host, host:port or http://host) without looking for the pad on USB first. The default is to find it on USB and use 192.168.7.1

      --timeout <SECS>
          How long to wait for the pad on USB after each reboot
          
          [default: 10]

      --no-channel
          Don't use the USB control channel (the gamepadii firmware's): only web-config and button presses

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
